<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to offer 5-yr bonds of HUF 5 bln on Feb 27.</title>
<headline>Hungary to offer 5-yr bonds of HUF 5 bln on Feb 27.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction five billion forints ($28.7 million) worth of the five-year government bonds of 2001/C series on February 27, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said.</p>
<p>    First day of interest period    3 February 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity		   12 December 2001</p>
<p>    Bills on offer			5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price			98.08 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum yield			    16.19 pct</p>
<p>Average yield of 2001/C</p>
<p>	bonds at last auction (Jan 30)   15.69 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 15.00 percent, payable semi-anually starting from June 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040' ($ = 174.1 Hungarian Forints)</p>
